{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":23588406,"ns":0,"title":"Vanilla humblotii","revisions":[{"revid":1314028723,"parentid":1194369795,"minor":false,"timestamp":"2025-09-29T09:44:34Z","size":2370,"sha1":"2c1a80d474d0523467357148822609b66026adbc","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|Species of orchid}}\n{{Speciesbox\n| image = Vanilla humblotii.jpg\n| image_caption = ''Vanilla humblotii'' illustration\n| genus = Vanilla\n| species = humblotii\n| authority = [[Rchb.f.]]\n| synonyms =\n}}\n\n'''''Vanilla humblotii''''' is a species of [[orchid]] [[endemism|endemic]] to [[Madagascar]] and the island of [[Grande Comore]] in the [[Comoros Islands]].  Both are  off Africa in the [[Indian Ocean]]. They are an endangered species, with a low population caused by anthropogenic activity. They live on dry, rocky mountains and in mesophilous forests. Vanilla humblotii have no leaves and are characterized by canary yellow flowers with a red velvet lip.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=  Andriamihaja |first1=Cathucia F |last2= Ramarosandratana |first2=Aro V|last3= Grisoni|first3=Michel|last4=Jeannoda|first4=Vololoniaina|last5= Besse|first5= Pascale| date= November 24, 2020 |title=The Leafless Vanilla Species-Complex from the South-West Indian Ocean Region: A Taxonomic Puzzle and a Model for Orchid Evolution and Conservation Research |url= https://res.mdpi.com/diversity/diversity-12-00443/article_deploy/diversity-12-00443.pdf|journal= Diversity|volume=12 |issue=12 |pages=443 |doi=10.3390/d12120443 |bibcode=2020Diver..12..443A |access-date= March 18, 2021|doi-access=free}}</ref> They are known to have applications in medicine due to its antimicrobial properties, so it is important to protect them for future use.<ref>{{cite journal |last1=Gigant |first1=R.|last2=De Bruyn |first2=A.|last3=M’sa|first3=T.|last4=Viscardi|first4= G.|last5=Gigord|first5=L.|last6=Gauvin-Bialecki|first6=A.|last7=Pailler|first7= T.|last8=Humeau|first8= L.|last9= Grisoni|first9=M.|last10=Besse|first10=P.|date= April 6, 2016|title= Combining pollination ecology and fine-scale spatial genetic structure analysis to unravel the reproductive strategy of an insular threatened orchid |journal= South African Journal of Botany|volume= 105|issue=2016 |pages= 25–35|doi= 10.1016/j.sajb.2016.02.205|bibcode=2016SAJB..105...25G |doi-access=free}}</ref>\n\n==References==\n{{Commons category|Vanilla humblotii|position=left}}\n{{Wikispecies|position=left|Vanilla humblotii}}\n{{Reflist}}\n\n{{Taxonbar|from=Q2890768}}\n\n[[Category:Vanilla|humblotii]]\n[[Category:Orchids of Africa]]\n[[Category:Orchids of Madagascar]]\n[[Category:Flora of the Comoros]]\n\n\n{{Vanilloideae-stub}}"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-10-26T19:42:01Z","lastrevid":1314028723,"length":2370}]}}